## Verdict

Blaxel Go/TS examples (27/27) and provider/core READMEs are in good shape. The real miss is **TypeScript `SandboxInfo` / error field parity with Go**: `createdAt`, `providerMetadata`, and `providerSource`.

---

## Standards

### Hard
- **`sdks/typescript/providers/blaxel/src/errors.ts`** — never sets `providerSource`. Go maps `BlaxelSource` / `Origin`; Daytona TS sets `providerSource`. Cites `docs/responses-and-errors.md` and cross-language error parity in `docs/provider-verification.md`.

### Judgement
- Misleading comment in `mappings.ts`: “Idle first (matches Go)” while both languages map **maximumLifetime first**.
- Process wait timeout keyed off message prefix `"Process did not finish in time"`.
- Create rejection copy uses “not mapped” (same as Daytona; audience rule prefers “not supported”).

### Clean
- Create/config checks, TTL/idle floors, Http2Tls, reserved ports align Go↔TS.
- Install commands (`@sandbox-kit/blaxel`, `…/providers/blaxel`) are consistent across root + provider READMEs.

---

## Spec

### Missing / partial
1. **TS `providerSource`** — `docs/responses-and-errors.md`: carry `ProviderSource` when the provider sent it.
2. **TS drops `createdAt` / `providerMetadata`** that Go `metadata.go` fills — conflicts with “preserve field presence” in `AGENTS.md`. Tests currently lock the omission in.

### Scope creep
- New docs-audience rule/skill churn beyond the provider itself.
- Go `ProviderMetadata` bag is richer than YAML `mapSandboxInfo` field list (still reasonable vs Daytona).

### Wrong / inconsistent
- Website shapes still advertise `providerState?` in places (audience rule: don’t surface unless callers must read it).
- Same create/get/refresh path yields unequal `SandboxInfo` across languages.

---

## SDKs, examples, READMEs

### What’s solid
| Area | Status |
| --- | --- |
| Example catalog | 27 Go ↔ 27 TS names match; catalogs list all |
| Spot-checked examples | create / errors / delete / timeout / stat APIs correct |
| Provider READMEs | Install, create, lifecycle, FS, process, error kinds align |
| Root + sandbox READMEs | Blaxel install and env (`BL_*`) correct |
| Error **kinds** (codes/status) | Go↔TS maps match (409 create → AlreadyExists, POLICY_VIOLATION, LOCKDOWN_ERROR, …) |
| Create validation | name/image/resources/domains/ports/lifetime/Http2Tls parity |

### Fix 1 — Port Go metadata into TS (highest priority)

Go fills these on get/refresh; TS `mapSandboxInfo` does not, and the test asserts that:

```566:567:sdks/typescript/providers/blaxel/src/blaxel.test.ts
    expect(info.createdAt).toBeUndefined();
    expect(info.providerMetadata).toBeUndefined();
```

`@blaxel/core` already exposes what you need (`metadata.displayName` / `createdAt` / `updatedAt`, `lastUsedAt`, `expiresIn`). Widen the identity type and project like Daytona TS / Go `metadata.go`:

```ts
// provider_mappings.ts — widen BlaxelSandboxIdentity
export interface BlaxelSandboxIdentity {
  readonly metadata?: {
    readonly name?: string;
    readonly labels?: Readonly<Record<string, string>>;
    readonly displayName?: string;
    readonly createdAt?: string;
    readonly updatedAt?: string;
  };
  readonly status?: unknown;
  readonly state?: unknown;
  readonly lastUsedAt?: string;
  readonly expiresIn?: number;
  readonly nodeGeneration?: string;
  readonly spec?: {
    readonly region?: string;
    readonly runtime?: { readonly memory?: number };
  };
}
```

```ts
// mappings.ts — after resources in mapSandboxInfo
const values: Record<string, MetadataValue> = {};
assignText(values, "display_name", value.metadata?.displayName);
assignText(values, "created_at", value.metadata?.createdAt);
assignText(values, "updated_at", value.metadata?.updatedAt);
assignText(values, "last_used_at", value.lastUsedAt);
assignText(values, "node_generation", value.nodeGeneration);
if (value.expiresIn !== undefined && value.expiresIn > 0) {
  values.expires_in_seconds = { signedInteger: BigInt(value.expiresIn) };
}
const runtime = value.state !== undefined ? String(value.state) : "";
if (runtime !== "") values.runtime_state = { text: runtime };
if (Object.keys(values).length > 0) {
  mutable(result).providerMetadata = { values };
}
const created = value.metadata?.createdAt;
if (created) {
  const date = new Date(created);
  if (!Number.isNaN(date.valueOf())) mutable(result).createdAt = date;
}
```

Also update `projectHandle` to pass through `lastUsedAt` / `expiresIn` / `nodeGeneration` from `SandboxInstance`.

### Fix 2 — Set `providerSource` on TS errors

Go reads `X-Blaxel-Source` then body `origin`. TS can mirror without a core helper:

```ts
function blaxelProviderSource(error: unknown): string | undefined {
  const header = /* response.headers.get("x-blaxel-source") */;
  if (header) return header;
  for (const body of [error, (error as any)?.error, (error as any)?.data]) {
    const origin =
      typeof body?.origin === "string" ? body.origin :
      typeof body?.error?.origin === "string" ? body.error.origin : undefined;
    if (origin) return origin;
  }
  return undefined;
}

// in create() / mapBlaxelError:
...(providerSource === undefined ? {} : { providerSource }),
```

Same pattern as Daytona TS `error.source`.

### Fix 3 — Small README / comment hygiene

**TS `stat-blaxel-file` README** — add the Go twin’s size note:

```md
`name` and `path` are whatever Blaxel reports. Size may be zero when Blaxel
does not return it.
```

**`mappings.ts` comment** — replace “Idle first” with reality:

```ts
// Maximum lifetime first, then idle (matches Go creation.go).
```

### Not worth chasing for Blaxel alone
- Go `RejectUnmapped` vs TS known-unsupported only — same as Daytona/Modal TS.
- Provider-layer empty `argv` guard in Go only — shared process validation covers TS.

---

**Standards:** 1 hard (`providerSource`), ~3 soft. Worst: missing `providerSource`.  
**Spec:** 2 missing (metadata + `providerSource`), 1 docs-voice inconsistency. Worst: TS `SandboxInfo` thinner than Go.

I can apply Fix 1–3 on this branch if you want.

